# The pointer theme of the system (docs/POINTERS.md, section 5), under the
# license of the repository. Each shape is an outline: closed contours of
# lines and quadratic curves in layers. A contour of a layer "fill" or of an
# accent is the whole shape: the tool draws an edge of 1 pixel inside it at
# every size, then the fill. The theme file holds two forms: a white fill in
# a dark edge for a dark desktop, a dark fill in a white edge for a light one.
#
# A unit is a pixel at the size 24: an integer coordinate is a pixel corner,
# so each level and upright edge is sharp at 24 and at 48. A contour is 2
# units wider than its fill: a stroke of 1 pixel of fill is 3 units wide.
# Two contours of one layer that must join overlap by 2 units; two fingers
# overlap by 1, which parts their fills by 1 pixel at 24 only where both
# stand free above the palm. A line of edge of half a unit parts them at 48.
# The option "hot" is the pixel that points, at 24. The centre of a
# symmetric shape is the pixel 11.
#
# The loaders of wait and busy_with_arrow are made by a computation of the
# arcs, written here as its result: 16 frames of 60 ms, one turn in 960 ms;
# in each frame a bright arc of a quarter turn with a round head, then three
# arcs of an eighth of a turn behind it at 70, 45 and 20 percent of the
# blue of the focus, the rest of the ring the fill.
#
# See the sheet of every shape with: modustool pointers preview <file.png>
theme System
license MIT
attribution The pointer theme of the system, drawn as outlines in resources/pointers/system.manifest.

sizes 24 48

# The arrow: a large head and a short tail. The point on the corner 1,1;
# the left side upright, 18 pixels; the right side at 45 degrees to the
# wing at 14,14, so the head is 13 wide. The notch 6,14 is deep, level with
# the wing, so the head reads as one triangle. The tail is a parallelogram
# along the axis of the arrow, 2 down for 1 across: it leaves the head
# between the notch and the point 10,14, is 4 across (1.6 pixels of fill),
# 4.5 long, and its end 8,18 to 11.2,16.4 is square to the axis.
shape arrow hot 1 1
layer fill
contour 1 1 line 1 19 line 6 14 line 8 18 line 11.2 16.4 line 10 14 line 14 14

# An I-beam: a stem of 1 pixel, bars that pass it by 2 pixels on each side.
shape text hot 11 11
layer fill
contour 8 3 line 15 3 line 15 6 line 8 6
contour 8 17 line 15 17 line 15 20 line 8 20
contour 10 4 line 13 4 line 13 19 line 10 19

# A slender hand: the index finger of 3 pixels of fill, 9 pixels above the
# knuckles; three folded fingers as distinct rounded bumps, each lower by
# 1.5 or 2 pixels. The palm starts at 11, so two bumps are parted by a dip
# of 1 or 2 pixels at their tops, not by a line down the hand; only the
# index finger is parted from them further. The palm has rounded lower
# corners and narrows to a wrist of 7; the thumb is a rounded bump at the
# left, at the height of the folded fingers. At 48 one line of edge parts
# the index finger from the folded fingers, as at 24.
shape pointing_hand hot 8 1
layer fill
contour 6 15 line 6 3.5 curve 6 1 8.5 1 curve 11 1 11 3.5 line 11 15
contour 10 15 line 10 9 curve 10 7 12 7 curve 14 7 14 9 line 14 15
contour 13 15 line 13 10.5 curve 13 8.5 15 8.5 curve 17 8.5 17 10.5 line 17 15
contour 16 15 line 16 11.5 curve 16 10 17.5 10 curve 19 10 19 11.5 line 19 15
contour 6 11 line 19 11 line 19 15 curve 19 17 17.5 18 line 16 21 line 9 21 line 7.5 18 curve 6 17 6 15
contour 8 9 line 6 9 curve 4 9 4 11 curve 4 13 6 13 line 8 13
layer edge
contour 10.5 8 line 11 8 line 11 11.5 line 10.5 11.5

# An open hand: four fingers of 2 pixels of fill, 1 pixel apart above the
# palm only: the palm starts at 8, so each gap is as long as the free part
# of its fingers, not the whole hand. The palm has rounded lower corners
# and narrows to a wrist of 7; the thumb is a bump at the left.
shape grab hot 11 12
layer fill
contour 5 13 line 5 7 curve 5 5 7 5 curve 9 5 9 7 line 9 13
contour 8 13 line 8 5 curve 8 3 10 3 curve 12 3 12 5 line 12 13
contour 11 13 line 11 6 curve 11 4 13 4 curve 15 4 15 6 line 15 13
contour 14 13 line 14 8 curve 14 6 16 6 curve 18 6 18 8 line 18 13
contour 5 8 line 18 8 line 18 14 curve 18 17 16 18 line 15 20 line 8 20 line 7 18 curve 5 17 5 14
contour 7 11 line 5 11 curve 3 11 3 13 curve 3 15 5 15 line 7 15
layer edge
contour 8.5 6 line 9 6 line 9 8.5 line 8.5 8.5
contour 11.5 5 line 12 5 line 12 8.5 line 11.5 8.5
contour 14.5 7 line 15 7 line 15 8.5 line 14.5 8.5

# The same hand closed: the fingers curled to four distinct rounded
# knuckles. The palm starts at 10, so two knuckles are parted by a dip of 2
# or 3 pixels at 24, not by a line down the hand; at 48 a short line of
# edge marks each dip.
shape grabbing hot 11 13
layer fill
contour 5 14 line 5 10 curve 5 8 7 8 curve 9 8 9 10 line 9 14
contour 8 14 line 8 9 curve 8 7 10 7 curve 12 7 12 9 line 12 14
contour 11 14 line 11 9 curve 11 7 13 7 curve 15 7 15 9 line 15 14
contour 14 14 line 14 10 curve 14 8 16 8 curve 18 8 18 10 line 18 14
contour 5 10 line 18 10 line 18 14 curve 18 17 16 18 line 15 20 line 8 20 line 7 18 curve 5 17 5 14
contour 7 12 line 5 12 curve 3 12 3 14 curve 3 16 5 16 line 7 16
layer edge
contour 8.5 9 line 9 9 line 9 10.5 line 8.5 10.5
contour 11.5 8 line 12 8 line 12 10.5 line 11.5 10.5
contour 14.5 9 line 15 9 line 15 10.5 line 14.5 10.5

# Four compact heads, near equilateral, on shafts of 1 pixel.
shape move hot 11 11
layer fill
contour 10 5 line 13 5 line 13 18 line 10 18
contour 5 10 line 18 10 line 18 13 line 5 13
contour 11.5 1.5 line 14.675 7 line 8.325 7
contour 11.5 21.5 line 8.325 16 line 14.675 16
contour 1.5 11.5 line 7 8.325 line 7 14.675
contour 21.5 11.5 line 16 14.675 line 16 8.325

